@jodiecongirl GLP-1= Semaglutide (Ozempic &amp; Wegovy): reduces appetite, slows digestion. 

Dual agonist GLP-1 + GIP= Tirzepatide (Mounjaro &amp; Zepbound): as above + lowers blood sugar, manages fat deposition (burning more fat).

So neither of them just work on appetite.

@muscleforlife Me 3 years ago: Trainer. Dietician. Followed everything for 6 months tracking every lick &amp; sniff of food. Lost 10lbs.

Added: Endocrinologist. started me on Wegovy, I continued the same training/diet. Weight started falling off. 

Now you understand what people are paying for 🙄

@FamilyFeud 

Why do these women sorry but most of them are African-American women are so big like fat while there’s so many things now that can help you lose weight I took Wegovy I lost 30 pounds in six months 
What’s the problem with these people

@sweetcarolinatv ... around 15% in studies.
Ozempic (Semaglutide): The same active ingredient as Wegovy (semaglutide) but FDA-approved for Type 2 Diabetes; often used off-label for weight loss.
Saxenda (Liraglutide): A daily injection used to manage weight by controlling appetite

@JonahLupton The gelatine acts as a Satiety effect to make you feel full as glp-1 would.
I tried the Wegovy 4 MG dosages for 3 weeks and quit from the Nauseous / sick feeling

I know from my experience!!!! Jonah, you would not take either pill or shot, so I dont believe in them! Lost 8 pounds

@drmarlonperalta Gained 22 lbs. on Semaglutide.  Hungry all the time.

Lost 170 lbs. on Tirzepatide.  Hunger is manageable.

Cannot stand even the smell of food with Retatrutide.  Eating is a chore.

@HatedMoats The Wegovy pill is actually superior in efficacy and tolerability. It could be a big game changer.

There are lots of people who are overweight, not obese and just want to lose 10-20 lbs. The pill is greated for that. 

It reshapes the weightloss mkt.

@parmita This is pretty low-dose for oral semaglutide.

Which is par for the course for Lilly. Part of their efficacy trick is comparing, eg, 15mg tirz to 1mg sema.

By contrast, the cagrisema trial that just happened used max dose tirz and lost.

@achilleas_ghost Ehhh last week was a new record for highest sales ever of Wegovy/ozempic./Rybelsus/Mounjaro/Zepbound/ Trulicity. 

So yes doctors will gladly prescribe FDA APPROVED glp1. 

But not all those non approved grey market peptides

@VinnyJay87 @fdzmurillo Foundayo: concerns about drug interactions at higher doses.
Patients using statins must cap their statin dosis: Simvastatin limited at 20mg with Foundayo.
Wegovy pill holds a stronger profile for patients on statins due to its established cardiovascular risk reduction benefits.

@BrandonLuuMD I had a wave of tirzepatide &amp; semaglutide side effect patients in the ER this week. 
3 of them there for the third time vomiting &amp; responsive to gastroparesis-like interventions. 2 had lowered doses and still felt horrible. 

Curious of the side effect &amp; Rx abandonment rates

@brian_blum1 You can get real Wegovy for $150/mo. 

Why are people paying $200/mo to these gray market dealers for compounded sema? Many of the patients using these sites aren't even getting Tirzepatide or dual agonists lol.

They're just overcharging using deceptive payment schemes

