@JAMA obesity &amp; cancer review: GLP-1 RAs (semaglutide/tirzepatide) → ~10–15% wt loss. 

Observational data suggest modest ↓ obesity-related cancers; in 1.65M T2D pts vs insulin: pancreas HR 0.41, liver 0.47, CRC 0.54. RCTs still needed. 

#GLP1 #Oncology @kubilaykarsidag https://t.co/51Yr62DiNv

@Tirzepjunkie @Ashwinreads Oral Wegovy is more efficacious with fewer side effects.

Plus we know way less about long-term side effects of Foundayo.  The label has all sorts of restrictions (including on Simvastatin) for a reason.  

Peptides may be inherently better in obesity than small molecules.

